Define _XOPEN_SOURCE as 700 on QNX, as on FreeBSD.

config.h defines a bare "#define _XOPEN_SOURCE" (no value) on every system
it does not know. QNX's <sys/platform.h> accepts only the values 500, 600
and 700 and stops with "#error This version of XOPEN_SOURCE is not
supported" otherwise. 700 is the X/Open level that goes with the
_POSIX_C_SOURCE 200809L config.h asks for, and what QNX 8 implements; it is
what FreeBSD gets already.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/cmake/config.h.in
+++ b/cmake/config.h.in
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 
 #if defined(__SunOS_5_8) || defined(__SunOS_5_9) || defined(__SunOS_5_10)
 #  define _XOPEN_SOURCE 500
-#elif defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#elif defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__QNX__)
 #  define _XOPEN_SOURCE 700
 #elif defined(__ibmxl__) && defined(__clang__) // Compiler xlclang
 #  define _XOPEN_SOURCE 600
